      "text": "%pyspark\n# Step 1: Transform entire catalog to get features and hashes\ncatalog_vec \u003d model.transform(ml_df).cache()\n\n# Step 2: Extract normalized vector of the query product\nquery_id \u003d 12345  # Replace with an actual product ID from your catalog\nquery_vector_row \u003d catalog_vec.filter(catalog_vec.id \u003d\u003d query_id).select(\"product_name_vec\").head()\n\nif query_vector_row is None:\n    print(f\"Product ID {query_id} not found in catalog.\")\nelse:\n    query_vector \u003d query_vector_row[0]\n\n    # Step 3: Find top 5 nearest neighbors using LSH model (last stage in pipeline)\n    lsh_model \u003d model.stages[-1]\n    recommendations \u003d lsh_model.approxNearestNeighbors(catalog_vec, query_vector, 6)  # 6 because query itself included\n\n    # Step 4: Filter out the query product itself from results\n    recommendations_filtered \u003d recommendations.filter(recommendations.id !\u003d query_id)\n\n    # Step 5: Show top 5 recommendations\n    recommendations_filtered.select(\"id\", \"distCol\").show(5)",
